      content:
          'A 30-year-old transgender woman (male sex assigned at birth, female gender identity) is admitted to acute inpatient rehabilitation following a T6 ASIA A complete spinal cord injury sustained in a motorcycle accident 3 weeks ago. She underwent posterior spinal fusion T4-T8 and had an uncomplicated post-operative course. She has been on feminizing hormone therapy (estradiol and spironolactone) for 4 years through an endocrinology clinic and has not undergone gender-affirming surgery. Her legal name has been changed and her insurance and identification documents reflect her female name and gender marker. She presents to the rehab unit appearing anxious. She tells the admitting nurse, "I need to know that I will be treated with respect here. My last hospital experience was terrible — they kept calling me \'he\' and put me in a room with a man." She is accompanied by her partner (cisgender female) and her mother, who is supportive.',
