    Section(
      title: 'History & Systems Review:',
      content:
          '**Past Medical History:** No significant medical history prior to SCI. On feminizing hormone therapy since age 26. No history of DVT or thromboembolic events. No surgical history prior to spinal fusion.\n\n**Hormone Therapy Regimen:**\n- Estradiol valerate 20 mg IM every 2 weeks (last injection 10 days ago)\n- Spironolactone 100 mg BID\n- Duration: 4 years with good feminization (breast development Tanner III, redistribution of body fat, reduced facial hair growth)\n\n**SCI Details:** T6 ASIA A complete paraplegia. No sacral sparing. Neurogenic bladder (indwelling Foley catheter, planned transition to intermittent catheterization). Neurogenic bowel (digital stimulation program to be initiated). At risk for autonomic dysreflexia (T6 level).\n\n**Current Medications:** Estradiol valerate 20 mg IM q2 weeks, spironolactone 100 mg BID, gabapentin 300 mg TID (neuropathic pain), docusate/senna, subcutaneous heparin, famotidine.\n\n**Psychiatric History:** Treated gender dysphoria with hormone therapy. History of anxiety and depression (in remission on hormone therapy). No active psychiatric medications. Reports significant distress about how she will be treated in rehab setting.\n\n**Social History:** Works as a graphic designer (remote work — can resume from wheelchair). Lives with partner in an accessible apartment (first floor, one step to enter). Supportive mother. Father is estranged (rejected her after transition). Strong friend network in the LGBTQ+ community. Has health insurance through employer.',
